From bb00d86a5f3d9fc59a4661b6c1d218569ee46824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: webby <webby@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:52:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Windows port: pace rendering updates by the display, at
 its real refresh rate

Rendering updates were paced by a 16ms run loop timer. A timer drifts against
the display, so frames reached the screen at uneven intervals, and it cannot
follow a display that is not 60Hz. DisplayRefreshMonitorWin now waits for the
desktop compositor to present (DwmFlush) on a thread of its own and reports the
display's refresh rate, and the UI process tells pages that rate, without which
a page assumes 60Hz.
